Description: "3D display settings..." starts KScreen's page on the desktop session's platform
 kcmshell6 was started with Jmol's environment; with QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb in it inside a Wayland session, KScreen's
 page asked for the X11 backend, whose service aborted, and the page said that no KScreen backend was found. It is now
 started without QT_QPA_PLATFORM, so the page follows the session.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
---
--- a/src/org/openscience/jmol/app/jmolpanel/Stereo3D.java
+++ b/src/org/openscience/jmol/app/jmolpanel/Stereo3D.java
@@ -318,7 +318,11 @@
   /** Open the desktop's display settings (KScreen), where a screen's 3D mode and the depth limits are set. */
   public static void openDisplaySettings(Component parent) {
     try {
-      new ProcessBuilder("kcmshell6", "kcm_kscreen").start();
+      // KScreen's page follows the desktop session: started with QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb inside a Wayland session it asks
+      // for the X11 backend, which aborts, and the page has no display to show.
+      ProcessBuilder settings = new ProcessBuilder("kcmshell6", "kcm_kscreen");
+      settings.environment().remove("QT_QPA_PLATFORM");
+      settings.start();
     } catch (Exception e) {
       tell(parent, "settings", tr("settingsFailed"), e.getMessage());
     }
